 html←DemoteHeadings html;pat;rep
⍝ Shifts every heading in `html` down one level, H1 becoming H2 and so on, with H6 staying
⍝ as it is because there is nowhere further to go.
⍝ A README starts at H1, which on a package page would compete with the page's own H1. The
⍝ page keeps one H1 of its own and the README sits below it, which is both what a reader
⍝ expects and what a search engine wants to see.
⍝ One ⎕R with a pattern per level rather than six passes: ⎕R does not rescan what it has
⍝ replaced, so H1 cannot be shifted to H2 by the first pattern and then to H3 by the second.
 pat←'<h1' '<h2' '<h3' '<h4' '<h5' '<h6'
 pat,←'</h1' '</h2' '</h3' '</h4' '</h5' '</h6'
 rep←'<h2' '<h3' '<h4' '<h5' '<h6' '<h6'
 rep,←'</h2' '</h3' '</h4' '</h5' '</h6' '</h6'
 html←pat ⎕R rep⍠('IC' 1)⊣html
⍝Done
